    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d698">

                <pb facs="0909" n="897" sameAs="frus:frus1946v07/pg897"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68110/11–146: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-11-01T11:00:00+02:00">November 1,
                            1946—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1154. British Ambassador told me last night informed by Peterson at Moscow
                    Soviets have replied to recent British note on Straits in sense Soviets do not
                    consider discussions with Turks as ended and do not consider opportune convoke
                    international conference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
